these scripts are here to help us load main mem with just a sample x86_32 program or hard coded binary

some paramaters: 
main mem is 32kb, broken into 64 banks, which are each borken in to 4 sepereate memCell modules
these memCell modules are the ones that will be loaded with .hex files with readmemh calls in a tb
whats weird about the mem is that it is interleaved so its now sequetial, however it is not interleaved
at the $line level. cache line is 16B. so $line_0 will be in bank_0 and $line_1 in bank_1, due to the 
number of banks, $line_63 will be in bank_63 and $line_64 will be in bank_0. Futhermore, there are (2^15/2^4)
total $lines. with the sizing params given, each bank will have 32 $lines bc 2^11/2^6 bc 64 banks. now, each bank's 
32 $lines need to split into 4 seperate chunk, st the first 4 bytes of each $line goes into the first memcell, and the 
subsequently the same for the next three chunks and cell. 

here is the pipeline

first take an x86_32 pogram that will be passed in a json file contains a code and data section, which will look like

.org x1000
.code 
{code}

.org x2000
.data
{data stuff}

and convert it into a binary, note that all bytes that are not used need to be able to be randomzed to simulate real dram, so if some kind of flag
is set, then randomize it

then, it needs to be divided up into the interleaved banks
then it needs to be split into 4 chunks

then each files need to be create kind of like mem_{bankNum}_{chunkNum}.hex
these files need to be outputed to a output dir that will be passed in throuhg the json file

during this process somethings need to be created to help me debug
first after the program is "compiled", a human readable hex file needs ot be create of the whole program where the $line numver and starting addr is specifed then the $line is written
there also needs to be hex file just of code and data section, which also still show the cacheilne number and starting address of the line

note all of this needs to use readmemh and not binary. so the output of the "compile" step will be a big .hex file, then the createing the loadble hex files is also a bunch of .hex files
split this into two scripts, compile, and genHexMem
